# @corpus current
# gap[082] — the composition law must REFUSE a silently-lossy derivation.
#
# The same four edges as `examples/conversion/relation.id`, over i64 instead of
# f64. That one change makes each division NARROWING — 25401 micron is not a
# whole inch — and the class lattice must therefore refuse `inch -> milli`,
# which is a route it can plainly see.
#
# WHY THIS FIXTURE IS THE IMPORTANT HALF. An algebra that composes ANYTHING is
# not safer than no algebra; it is more dangerous, because adding one
# descriptor could quietly change an existing program's answer. The refusal is
# what makes the mechanism safe to scale, and it costs real derivations: the
# f64 fixture derives 6 edges from 6 authored, this one derives 0 from 4 and
# reports 2 refused. Both numbers are the same law.
#
# The diagnostic names the WEAK HOP, not just the pair, because "no conversion"
# would send the reader looking for a missing edge when the edge is present and
# the CLASS is the objection.
#
# The filename keeps a `_` because every fixture in this directory does; the
# harness matches on the path.

stretch = (v: i64): i64
    v * 25400

shrink = (v: i64): i64
    v // 25400

swell = (v: i64): i64
    v * 1000

shrivel = (v: i64): i64
    v // 1000

to(micron)(inch) = stretch@exact
to(inch)(micron) = shrink@narrowing
to(micron)(milli) = swell@exact
to(milli)(micron) = shrivel@narrowing

main = (): i64
    # THE CALL SITE MUST NAME THE SOURCE, or there is no `inch -> milli` to
    # refuse. `5:to(milli)` was substituted here in the FROM-ZERO sweep with a
    # note that the `inch` source would arrive "from binding context when
    # nominal descriptor lands (GAP-097)". GAP-097 has not landed, so `5` is a
    # bare i64 and the lossy route is never requested: the file stopped
    # expressing its own subject and went green. Measured on the repaired
    # spelling:
    #
    #     milli.from(inch)(5)  -> no silent conversion inch -> milli:
    #                             derived inch -> milli via micron
    #     5:to(milli)(inch)    -> emits C calling an undeclared lua_to_num
    #     5:to(milli)          -> same, and names no source at all
    #     milli:from(inch)(5)  -> 'from' is neither a descriptor nor a callable
    #
    # `dest.from(src)(v)` is the spelling `emit_relation_convert` documents as
    # naming the source (spec 2.6 gate 6), and it is the only one of the four
    # that reaches the class lattice. The colon face of the same edge is a
    # separate front-end defect and is not this fixture's subject.
    bore: i64 = milli.from(inch)(5)
    print("{bore}")
    0
